  "description": "ETOCAV crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C139 H93 Dy4 N2 O23 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,2(C1 H4 O1),2.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.740-3.851 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.07-110.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Et3NH][Dy4(ana)9(OH)4(CH3CN)2(H2O)]·3.5CH3CN·CH3OH (Hana = anthracene-9-carboxylic acid); EA C153H123.5Dy4N6.5O24. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
